# Purpose

This document defines how information is structured, organized and accessed throughout the Aura Platform.

A good information architecture reduces cognitive load.

Users should always know:

• Where they are
• What they can do
• Where to go next

Without thinking.

---

# Navigation Philosophy

Aura is built around experiences.

Users should rarely browse devices.

Instead they interact with rooms, scenes and activities.

The hierarchy is intentionally shallow.

Maximum navigation depth is three levels.

---

# Application Structure

Aura

├── Home
├── Rooms
├── Scenes
├── Automations
├── Devices
├── Diagnostics
└── Settings

Everything begins from Home.

---

# Primary Navigation

The bottom navigation consists of five tabs.

1. Home
2. Rooms
3. Scenes
4. Devices
5. Settings

Diagnostics is accessed from Settings or through contextual error messages.

---

# Home

Purpose

Provide an immediate overview of the home.

Contains

• Suggested Actions
• Current Activity
• Favorite Devices
• Room Overview
• Recent Activity
• Active Scenes
• Alerts
• Quick Controls

The Home screen should answer:

"What should I do right now?"

