# Content Hierarchy

Every screen follows

Primary Content

↓

Primary Action

↓

Secondary Information

↓

Contextual Actions

↓

Technical Details

This order must never change.

---

# Relationships

Rooms contain Devices.

Devices participate in Scenes.

Scenes trigger Automations.

Automations control Devices.

Diagnostics monitors everything.

---

# Data Flow

User

↓

Intent

↓

Aura Core

↓

Relevant Module

↓

Connected Device

↓

Response

↓

Updated Interface

The user never interacts directly with hardware APIs.

---

# Context Awareness

Aura continuously evaluates

Current Room

Current Time

Current Activity

Connected Devices

Network Status

Recent Usage

Suggestions are generated from this context.

---

# Empty States

Every empty screen should guide the user.

Example

"No scenes yet.

Create your first scene to automate multiple devices with one tap."

Never display blank pages.

---

# Error Hierarchy

Minor Issues

Small inline messages.

Medium Issues

Banner notifications.

Critical Issues

Dedicated error screen with recovery steps.

---

# Notifications

Notifications should never interrupt ongoing interactions unless absolutely necessary.

Priority

Critical

Warning

Informational

Suggestions

Suggestions should always be dismissible.

---

# Future Expansion

The information architecture must support future modules without restructuring.

Examples

Energy Dashboard

Solar Panels

EV Charging

Weather

Presence Detection

Robot Vacuum

Security

Air Quality

These modules should integrate naturally into existing navigation.

---

# Navigation Principles

Users should never need to remember where something is.

Aura should make the destination feel obvious.

If users hesitate, the architecture should be reconsidered.

---

# Design Validation Checklist

Every screen must answer:

Where am I?

What can I do?

What is most important?

Can I go back easily?

Can I complete my task within two taps?

If any answer is "No", the navigation must be redesigned.

---

# IA Motto

Information should be discovered.

Never searched for.

